    "readmeSummary": "## X Tweet Scraper\n\nA web scraping Actor that extracts X (Twitter) content at scale: it collects tweets, replies, quote tweets, threads, profile posts, Lists and search results from URLs, handles, List IDs, Tweet IDs and free-text queries with extensive filter support. Technical capabilities include high-throughput paged reads, deduplication, language and date-window verification, stable conversation ordering, and targeted engagement reads (replies, quotes, retweeters, likers/favoriters, threads). The Actor returns rich structured data: full text (including long-form posts), timestamps, engagement metrics, public author profile metadata, nested quoted/retweeted posts, conversation identifiers, media with variants and metadata (images, videos, GIFs, alt text, sizes), disclosure and moderation labels, translations and embedded HTML, and optional article-level extraction. Outputs can be delivered as nested JSON or flattened spreadsheet-friendly rows with configurable field naming and column-mapping; runs include diagnostics and provenance information describing partial, empty or stopped extractions.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Feed tweet text, author metadata, media and engagement metrics into research, enrichment, analytics and AI training.\n- Build retrieval-augmented datasets and extract article bodies for RAG workflows.\n- Monitor brand mentions, track brand sentiment and collect product feedback from public posts.\n- Monitor competitor posts and industry terms for market or trend analysis.\n- Collect replies, quote tweets and full conversation threads for moderation or discourse analysis.\n- Find high-engagement or top-ranked posts by metric, date window or country for social performance research.\n- Bulk lookup of Tweet IDs and profile histories for dataset backfills and archival exports.\n- Export X data to CSV/Excel/JSON for downstream analysis, reporting or spreadsheets.\n- Discover prospects and public conversations for lead generation and outreach research.\n- Monitor topic-specific conversations (e.g., electric vehicles, AI agent tools) and build topic-focused datasets.",
